    "result_text": "The full suite passes. Only `AcceptanceTest` contains actual `@Test` methods (`AcceptanceBase` is abstract, `AuditLogCapture` is a helper), and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` behavior in the Spring PetClinic REST app. The `sharesHousehold` opt-in that *allows* a same-lastName + same-address owner already existed; the missing piece was assigning and returning a shared `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` field to the `Owner` response schema (regenerating `OwnerDto` with the field, which MapStruct auto-maps).\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `householdId` field mapped to the `household_id` column, with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`db/hsqldb`, `db/h2`, `db/mysql`, `db/postgres`) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table. Tests use hsqldb; the others keep the DBs consistent.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, after mapping, call new `assignHousehold(...)`:\n   - Only acts when `sharesHousehold` is true **and** an existing household member matches (same last name + address, compared case-insensitively with whitespace collapsed \u2014 reusing the existing `findHouseholdMembers`).\n   - Derives a **stable, deterministic** `householdId` (`HH-<12 hex>` from SHA-256 of the normalized last name + address) so every member of a household resolves to the same value regardless of creation order.\n   - Assigns it to the new owner and **backfills** existing members that lack it, so both/all household members share the identifier.\n\nThe acceptance test confirms two owners joining an existing owner's household (via `sharesHousehold`) both receive the same non-blank `householdId`.",
